  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly supports noun phrases after determiners, but several noun roots have very little matching mass there; this accounts for the near-zero probability of “needles” after “The” and also affects “pears” and “apples” in similar contexts. Add a general determiner-plus-optional-adjective context to those noun roots rather than encoding particular titles. Person names after “with” are also a recurring continuation, so give each available name root evidence for that visible context. Finally, the batch includes title-like prefixes ending in “PN and the N” followed by a paragraph break; a focused newline rule covers that structure without treating every noun as a paragraph boundary. These are provisional generalizations: determiners can precede adjectives or other noun choices, “with” need not introduce a person, and the title-like structure may continue in other contexts.",
